  "grammar_explanations": [
    {
      "slug": "imperatives: directions",
      "title_form": "Imperativos para dar direcciones",
      "title_target": "Imperatives for directions",
      "description_md_form": "Para dar direcciones en inglés, usamos el **imperativo**: la forma base del verbo sin sujeto. Es directo y claro.\n\n**Estructura:** `Verbo base + complemento`\n\n- `Get on the train.` (Sube al tren.)\n- `Get off at the airport.` (Bájate en el aeropuerto.)\n- `Get in the taxi.` (Métete en el taxi.)\n\nCon los verbos de movimiento, usamos **partículas** que cambian el significado:\n\n| Verbo | Significado |\n|-------|-------------|\n| `get on` | subir (a un vehículo grande) |\n| `get off` | bajar (de un vehículo) |\n| `get in` | subir / meterse (a un coche) |\n\nPara preguntar por una dirección, usamos el chunk: `Where is the gate?` (¿Dónde está la puerta?).",
      "description_md_target": "To give directions in English, we use the **imperative**: the base form of the verb without a subject. It is direct and clear.\n\n**Structure:** `Base verb + complement`\n\n- `Get on the train.`\n- `Get off at the airport.`\n- `Get in the taxi.`\n\nWith movement verbs, we use **particles** that change the meaning:\n\n| Verb | Meaning |\n|------|---------|\n| `get on` | to board (a large vehicle) |\n| `get off` | to leave (a vehicle) |\n| `get in` | to enter (a car) |\n\nTo ask for directions, use the chunk: `Where is the gate?`",
      "grammar_structure": "Base verb + complement",
      "conjugation_table": {
        "name": "imperative_directions",
        "headers": [
          "Verbo",
          "Uso",
          "Ejemplo"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "get on",
            "subir a un vehículo grande (tren, bus)",
            "Get on the train."
          ],
          [
            "get off",
            "bajar de un vehículo",
            "Get off at the airport."
          ],
          [
            "get in",
            "subir a un vehículo pequeño (taxi, coche)",
            "Get in the taxi."
          ]
        ]
      },
